  "details": "This issue only affect the local camera ghost but results in some entertainingly large/small cameras.\n\nSteps:\n\n1. wear an extremely large/small avatar as it's most noticeable at the extremes. scaling seems to work.\n\n2. quit and re-launch vrchat.\n\n3. open the camera and set anchor to local or world to view camera ghost\n\n4. it'll look normal at the size of the current avatar\n\n5. switch to a normal sized avatar and observe the camera being either too small or too big. \n\n6. this persists across worlds and until the play session ends.\n\nIncluded image of a normal sized camera ghost and extremely small/large ghosts for comparison.\n\nOnly tested this on PCVR so I am unsure if it affects other platforms/desktop.",
